        "comments": "The assembly of Lampanyctus crocodilus (fLamCro1) is based on 73X ONT data and 370X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. In total, 6 contigs were identified as contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral), totaling 0.138 Mb (with the largest being 0.044 Mb). Additionally, 1999 regions totaling 167.937 Mb (with the largest being 0.787 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. Mitochondrial genome was assembled using ptGAUL. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 110 haplotypic regions were removed, totaling 80.377Mb (with the largest being 2.163Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size",
